WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.392 --> 00:00:02.392
- You definitely don't need to be

00:00:02.392 --> 00:00:04.560
a lumberjack to be an ax-thrower.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.592
Anybody can do it, all shapes and sizes,

00:00:06.592 --> 00:00:09.683
men, women, all different kinds.

00:00:09.683 --> 00:00:12.266
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.329 --> 00:00:18.211
My name's Matt Wilson, we are at BATL,

00:00:18.211 --> 00:00:19.381
the Backyard Axe Throwing League,

00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:21.560
we're at the Toronto west location.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.970
- [Group] Remember proud
men, who only have—

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.032
- [Matt] BATL is a community based around

00:00:26.032 --> 00:00:28.141
the activity of ax-throwing.

00:00:28.141 --> 00:00:29.019
(horn)

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:29.852
What is ax-throwing?

00:00:29.852 --> 00:00:32.523
It's exactly that, it's throwing an ax

00:00:32.523 --> 00:00:34.101
at a target for points.

00:00:34.101 --> 00:00:36.321
Standard match format is
three rounds of five throws

00:00:36.321 --> 00:00:37.821
per round, and you have to win

00:00:37.821 --> 00:00:40.363
two out three rounds to win that match.

00:00:40.363 --> 00:00:41.253
It started with me learning how to

00:00:41.253 --> 00:00:42.541
throw an ax at a cottage.

00:00:42.541 --> 00:00:43.992
There's a whole lot of force up here,

00:00:43.992 --> 00:00:46.733
that's sort of how the
initial idea started

00:00:46.733 --> 00:00:48.592
and it was super addictive.

00:00:48.592 --> 00:00:50.523
This is like the culmination of many years

00:00:50.523 --> 00:00:53.453
of debauchery and boredom.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.912
Just straight up, like, I threw an ax

00:00:54.912 --> 00:00:57.539
and it was fun and we went from there.

00:00:57.539 --> 00:01:00.261
This is one of eight locations in Ontario

00:01:00.261 --> 00:01:03.563
and we have one in Alberta as well.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:05.163
We definitely didn't invent the activity,

00:01:05.163 --> 00:01:07.631
we just invented a different
way to do it that I think

00:01:07.631 --> 00:01:11.083
works a little better in
heavily-populated areas.

00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:12.552
Would I have started if
I didn't live in Canada,

00:01:12.552 --> 00:01:14.293
I don't know, I think
Toronto, it's a pretty

00:01:14.293 --> 00:01:16.981
world-class city that's
open to trying new things

00:01:16.981 --> 00:01:19.763
and taking on some new adventures

00:01:19.763 --> 00:01:23.053
and so people were very open-minded to it.

00:01:23.053 --> 00:01:25.483
I find a lot of people
in the city of Toronto

00:01:25.483 --> 00:01:28.763
that share values and ideals with myself

00:01:28.763 --> 00:01:30.922
and within BATL we try
to operate with a sense

00:01:30.922 --> 00:01:35.163
of fairness and acceptance
and equality across the board.

00:01:35.163 --> 00:01:37.003
We're already talking to
people overseas, people in

00:01:37.003 --> 00:01:40.443
Australia and Poland and
England, let alone the States.

00:01:40.443 --> 00:01:43.026
I think the sport can be huge.

